    rationale: Founder decision dialog after a 7-agent review
learnings:
  - 'The ''Guard 6.2%'' figure is the FLAG rate. Ground truth: 3 caught-later defects in 275 (~1.1%); merge-created defects 1/275 (0.36%), and Guard missed it while a blind LLM caught it. Never cite 6.2% as a defect rate.'
  - 'This repo''s Warpline shadow stream: 118 rows since 2026-07-17, 0 KNOTs, 115 auto-seal. The denominator is empty; only concurrency (a swarm) fills it.'
  - TD-2026-07-17-151 (native forge, git as checkpoint export, Guard Action = instrument) was nearly reversed by a team synthesis that never read it. Check standing founder directions before proposing a 'wedge'.
  - Warpline is PUBLIC (a-paradigm repo is public; @a-company/warpline 0.2.1 is on npm). The founder chose to keep it in Paradigm.
  - 'Paradigm multi-writer hazards: decision ids are random 1..999 and overwrite on collision; history ids are log line counts; tasks are gitignored; derived files are tracked. Fix ids (task T-2026-10-14-001d), not storage.'
  - 'Warpline stableKey = SymbolEntry.id, which is name-derived, so it is not rename-stable. renamed-from aliases and field-typed edges are load-bearing for per-domain admission: pull symbol-integrity Phase 2 items 3 and 4 ahead of Warpline M1.'
  - Architect and security disagreed on runner placement. The founder chose the home box; Aegis's controls are the floor.
