body: |-
  # Where things stand: 2026-10-14

  ## Shipped
  **7.15.0, Symbol Integrity Phase 1** (259b7903, branch feat/symbol-integrity, pushed; npm publish is the founder's).
  - One canonical entry per symbol; references resolved over all contributors.
  - Stubs are marked declared:false and reported as dangling.
  - resolveSymbol gives O(1), normalized lookup.
  - The MCP context is backed by the live index, with a debounced, atomic refresh. It needs an MCP restart to take effect.
  - reindex reloads first and rebuilds once.

  Phase 2 (T-2026-10-13-002) and Phase 3 (T-2026-10-13-003) are open. Phase 2's renamed-from aliases and typed edges are now prerequisites for Warpline per-domain admission.

  ## Warpline plan (TD-2026-10-14-735)
  - **Gate mode:** advisory by default. Fail closed only on gate, signal, aspect and pipeline contracts.
  - **Native-only:** projects are native Warpline (beta, heavy logging). Git is a milestone backup via the stake valve.
  - **Order:**
    1. Preconditions (T-2026-10-14-001): S1 identity, M0 ledger out of git, S4 custodian, Paradigm collision-free ids.
    2. Evidence (T-2026-10-14-002): outcome taxonomy, a 1,000-PR replay with pre-registered thresholds, a 2–3 agent shadow swarm.
    3. Server v1 (T-2026-10-14-003).
  - Expo is confirmation only. The 100-admission run is dropped.

  ## Server design (Fable architect)
  - **Process:** one warplined binary. It keeps its UDS listener and gains an HTTP/TLS face on handleRequest (server.ts:173).
  - **Storage:** files stay the record, with a derived SQLite index. A server registry holds repos, collaborators, visibility, webhooks, secrets and jobs; it is NOT history. Amend G4 to read "no forge-private storage of history or judgment".
  - **Repos:** each repo is one fabric at <dataRoot>/repos/<repoId>/.warpline. Agents run replica daemons, seal locally, and push bundles (the bundle protocol is new). admit and refs.advance run at home.
  - **New verbs:** refs.advance, knots.open, dag.slice, meaning.blame, meaning.log, delta.classify, sync.*, and a typed events WS.

  ## CI runner (Fable architect + Aegis)
  - **Pipelines:** .warpline/pipelines.yaml, read from the tree at the stateId. Required checks live in protected.json v2, which is human-class.
  - **Triggers:** admit (only when sealed, so a KNOT never runs), offer, ref.advance, release, schedule, manual.
  - **Witnesses:** results are signed testWitness:v1 records with a runner key, stored as a sidecar.
  - **Gated landing on protected refs:** seal, park in landing.jsonl, then refs.advance once required checks pass. CHECKS_FAILED refuses. An owner override is audited.
  - **v1 placement (founder):** home box, rootless containers.
  - **Aegis floor:**
    - Offer builds get no secrets and no network.
    - Changes to the pipeline file are gate-class, and protected runs use the base-ref pipeline.
    - Cache keys are bound to stateId and trust tier.
    - The runner key is separate from agent keys.
    - Default-deny egress through a registry proxy.
    - S4 must keep keys off any job-visible path.
    - Revisit placement (gVisor or Firecracker on a separate host) before any public repo.

  ## Console design (Atelier session 2026-10-14-warpline-console; .atelier/DESIGN.md)
  - **Structure:** an org dashboard leads to repo tabs (v1; the founder finds the look too generic, a v2 item).
  - **Inbox:** each repo opens on its Inbox, with a resizable live band that moves only on arrive, KNOT, or resolve. The Floor is its own tab.
  - **Decisions:** split-view.
  - **Access:** roles by domain (Owner, Developer, Observer). Agents never sign in.
  - **Look:** Control room dials 3·4·7, neutral human states, all on the preserved Warpline system.
  - **Open:** a failure colour, the v2 shell look, Offer threads.
  - **Gate:** the console build waits on F4.

  ## Demo
  ledgerette: a small TypeScript service, 4 agents through MCP, and one scripted plain-git developer. It runs on its own fabric, unseeded, and counts as the swarm evidence arm (excluded from K3 and from the replay).

  ## Shared docs
  - Scion vs Warpline (Claude Docs): https://claude.ai/code/artifact/cbbee6f6-e1bd-4b5d-b161-123e74cb8ee7
  - neurons: a:2026-10-14-docs-scion-vs-warpline-…; 8 neurons under ai/agents/source-control.

  ## Open founder items
  - npm publish of 7.15.0.
  - PR #47 (skills arc) is still open.
  - F4 ratification items (from older arcs).
